{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222926-mage-ascension-legacies","id":1222926,"title":"Mage Ascension - Legacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-29T09:35:23-07:00","id":1222926,"title":"Mage Ascension - Legacies","content":"Oh Hi!<br /> This is my first entry ever, its about an idea I had about the very essence of the Traditions on Ascension. My biggest issue is that to me, Traditions are quite weird, it talks about a traditional way o making magic, therefore developing groups dedicated to certain kinds of thought, philosophy and so on. HOWEVER, if you look closer they dont really make something unique at all, the nature of the avatar, true magick and paradigm makes so that each individual is a unique, which is good. The problem is that although in the fluff the Traditions are something important somehow at a &quot;magick level&quot; in reality they are not much more than politics, bureaucrats at most. It really annoys me that a group like Order of Hermes, having more than THOUSAND years of existence have not produced anything actually magical as a tradition other than: A) a Hogwarts in Mars, B) Reuniting the conception of magick in a concise system, C) Having grand respect for, who-knows-why, fairies.<br /> <br /> What is the MAGICK that Hermetics did that makes them unique? The Brotherhood of Akasha developed Do, which is not inherently magical, but the very pinnacle of their discipline, which is quite related to both their paradigm and magick without making them dependent of it. The Virtual Adepts may have not really created the Virtual Web but no one can argue their absurd close relations to such, as much as Totems to Khavadi are a thing specifically for them, not everyone else, or at least not that easy.<br /> <br /> For that, bear with me, for I tried something akin to the Legacies in Mage Awakeing. My people, I understand much of us quite dislike and hopes that somone starts an Index Prohibitorum and makes public pyres using Chronicles of Darkness, but that ideia of having groups with practices that are unique to each one is amazing, and they have like 140+ groups like that.<br /> <br /> Well, Legacies have a system, mechanics and fluff that are not really adequate to Ascension, but they can inspire something like them. So I came with a few Ideas and wrote those things below, I based it on the Mind's Eye Theatre book, although I never intended it or knew the existence of such books or their mechanics of Traditions boons to certain habilities hahahahah.<br /> <br /> So, here they are, coment what you think, hate as you want and hope my painful death, or may come up with your own ideias:<br /> <br /> <br /> People come here to present an idea and improvements to it with the help of the community.<br /> <br /> I have always wondered which magician had a great problem with the question of Traditions, because in fact these magician groups are a tradition only in the name and in the share of their used foci. That is, to be part if a Tradition is only made given to the stereotype and the sphere of specialization and not for other reasons what escapes of the plot of this group of mages.<br /> <br /> To try to solve this, I tried to take a look at other systems and I started to develop a house rule where each group of magicians would have a Legacy of Tradition, a real and tangible advantage to be and to continue in the group. Secrets.mystic developed by and for that organization.<br /> <br /> These are what I have mined on the books and remodeled so far:<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Ivory Tower' Mandate&quot;</b><br /> - Any of the agents of the Technocratic Union can enjoy the hegemony of the Scientific Consensus and be free of the possibility of paradox in using any technologies that are not alien to the current possibilities and even those speculated to exist (at storytellers discretion). The use of hypertechnology that is even short of conspiracy theories are not immune to paradox such as atomic disintegrators, dimensional or teleportation portals, indefinite extension of life (not aging, immortality, etc.).<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Oh, I can feel it!&quot;</b><br /> Members of the Cult of Ecstasy have a completely unique and often paradoxical ethic and vision of the universe even among other magi. Their ability to sense reality and modify their understanding of Tellurian allow them to be with one of the active mystical perceptions continuously. Systemwise a mage can choose a sphere she possesses and for the rest of hes life have the effects of said perception active. Ex. Spirit Sphere will make the cultist always be able to see a certain interposition between the world of spirits and material; someone from the Entropy sphere will continually feel the flow of causality between the infinite relationships that are near.<br /> Obs: To cancel this effect, the Magician must necessarily go through a ritual or routine to limit the advanced perception of some sphere, and if he does not, the madness will always be at his door because goddamit if spirits can be clingy.<br /> <br /> <b>The One Song</b><br /> The Celestial Choir prays on the ideal that all is but a fragment of the True Self, the One, the ultimate god, for it is the very origin of divinity and everything else. This belief is so strong that the members of said tradition thinks they should work together so that His servants be in unity even amidst differences. This Idea coalesces in such a way that when one or more choristers works together they may attain greater proximity to the One, as they too focus their will but in one thing. Systemwise when at least two choristers do the same magick together they can cast with more power than alone, in such a way as if there was another ONE (pun inteded). The choristers must try to cast the same routine in unison, what does not mean mirroring each other, the result will be casting the said magick with one more dice and it wont add more even if you call the entire Tradition to help, however the price for such is quite obvious too. When the One Song is practiced a figure, as if a third person may become visible even to Sleepers, and this said figure may look almost transparent as if not material at all, resembling aspect of the routine used and the cultural references of the users. The choristers may think of this visage as a tiny spark of the One's manifestation, hermetics however thinks that its no more than resonance showing itself and that choristers thinks too much...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Blessing of The Great Mother&quot;</b><br /> -The connection of the Verbena with the Great Mother goes beyond the use of natural materials and inputs. A Verbena in performing a ceremony during a natural event of importance and necessarily close to it will not be capable of generating critical failure in the midst of this single ritual.<br /> Ex. A ritual during a Blood Moon, an eclipse, a volcanic eruption, a storm, a flood of great proportions.<br /> Obs .: The ritual must have some relation with the natural event and mainly its resonance, as well as it can not be caused by the Verbena itself or by magic of any type.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Restructuring the Static Paradigm&quot;</b><br /> &quot;A member of the Ether Society does not do magick, but performs the purest Science. An Etherite can be immunized from the shock of paradox created when a Sleeper sees one of his experiments if he can convict it in some way that that realized can be explained scientifically.<br /> Obs: Extremely vulgar procedures can not be explained.<br /> <br /> This next one was something for the Order of Hermes, I wanted a thing that evokes that fact that they are well, the leaders of the Council and therefore should have something powerfull as well, since they are the guys who studied magick so hard that they formulated the Sphere System and the Purple Paradigm and many other shit that even the Union still utilizes. Well I didnt like this one I made, too long and too close to Charms, and a copy + paste of Vancian Magic.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Protocol of Hermeticum Formulae&quot;</b><br /> <br /> - A hermetic magi has prolonged and endless studies of the magical theories of Porthos and Bonisagus allowing a unique perception of the mystical processes. This strenuous study of the Order of Hermes allowed the development of a limited but extremely functional magickal methodology. Once per session the character can use a pre-established routine without the need for a scroll at the cost of an effect completely limited by the amount of successes generated previously in the preparation of this mechanism. Due to its formation in the Forces Sphere it is very common that the magi of the Order have preference for some effect of attack in this area, although it is not a limiting in itself.<br /> <br /> Note I: the prepared effect must be a routine, that is, if the Magician is not familiar enough or has never done so before, a Protocol will not be formed.<br /> <br /> Obs II: a Protocol does not roll Arete at the moment of use, therefore it will be used only the results of the data obtained at the time of its creation.<br /> <br /> Obs III: a protocol is a quasi-static routine, so its use is by means of predetermined and fixed actions, evading or not obeying the commands that the magi established will generate a paradoxical effect applied to the Effect. Ex. A Protocol with the purpose of creating rain will be done on a long parchment that will be immersed in water while the hermetic recites the invocation of Archangel Uriel and bla bla bla, in case he fails it will rain blood or other things other than the intended.<br /> <br /> Obs IV: It is worth noting that although it is quite functional and pragmatic, the use of the Protocols is a call to the hubris of indiscriminate use and may generate dependent. The risk of producing an undesired result is spectacular even compared to a common effect in front of witnesses.<br /> <br /> Obs V: a Protocol will generate paradox in the same way as a routine if it is vulgar, the great advantage in it is that the mage wont have to spend time to activate the intended Effect.<br /> <br /> Obs VI: a Protocol can take advantage of physical objects such as containers, grimoires, books, scrolls, etc., but a magi who is not the Protocol creator can never use it because only the one that crafted it may. Protocols are not magical items, they are not transferable and although they are used in certain cases of quintessence expenditure they do so because the original routine would require or the absence of some of the materials that may be interchangeable by their use.<br /> <br /> Obs VII: The Protocol will be produced by means of a ritual in which the magician will use the routine in question and leave it ready for a later use and it is activated only by means of a formulaic magicka, that can only be activated by means of a rigid procedure. A wizard in case he fails or has weak results can not perform a new ritual to replace the current one, for a new Protocol it will be necessary to use the first one, even if it was a critical failure.<br /> <br /> Note VIII: A Protocol counts as an active effect, so it adds +1 to the difficulty modifiers for any subsequent Arete rolls.<br /> <br /> Obs IX: Yes they are overpower, it is not for nothing that the Order of Hermes is the Tradition that presides over the Council.<br /> <br /> Et cetera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","user":"menos125","date":". 05-29-2018, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T17:05:40-07:00","id":1223061,"title":"","content":"You might be interested in looking into the magic system for Dark Ages: Mage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T18:15:12-07:00","id":1223081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222926-mage-ascension-legacies?p=1223061#post1223061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might be interested in looking into the magic system for Dark Ages: Mage</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah I know those, I really like the idea of Pillars, but too much hassle for something I think should be easy to understand and use. You see, I only accept House Rules that makes the game lighter and faster, using Pillar system as Dark Ages makes the game rules way more convoluted than they already are, and I have seen people discussing this idea here, its interesting, but too complex for an already complex game.<br /> <br /> Oh and my grammar quite sucks huh, Im re-reading what I've posted and it looks really bad written. meh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T22:54:35-07:00","id":1223124,"title":"","content":"I think the more valuable thing in DA: M to look at are the Foundations; especially since they can be layered on top of normal Mage Arete without any significant issues.<br /> <br /> You can even borrow from Awakening more directly by using Attainments as a model for what characters might get as bonuses as Arete increases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:46:50-07:00","id":1223205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222926-mage-ascension-legacies?p=1223124#post1223124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the more valuable thing in DA: M to look at are the Foundations; especially since they can be layered on top of normal Mage Arete without any significant issues.<br /> <br /> You can even borrow from Awakening more directly by using Attainments as a model for what characters might get as bonuses as Arete increases.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that. Instead of a single bonus you get from joining, you would have a whole &quot;spiritual path&quot; defined for each Tradition that gets more rewarding (and more distinct) the more a mage enlightens herself into the esoteric myteries of her Tradition's brand of magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:35:13-07:00","id":1223268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222926-mage-ascension-legacies?p=1223205#post1223205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I second that. Instead of a single bonus you get from joining, you would have a whole &quot;spiritual path&quot; defined for each Tradition that gets more rewarding (and more distinct) the more a mage enlightens herself into the esoteric myteries of her Tradition's brand of magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with Attainments is that they work in a very different way in Ascension than in Awakening, mainly the idea of chaging one own soul to follow a Path and paradox not happening If you use certain Effects. <br /> <br /> You see my main Idea is giving something unique to the major Mage groups without making It mandatory or making it so that the player must follow an specific way of background, paradigm or so on. Like, If you are an Hermetic using my Idea of Protocol and Formulaic Magic, you may use it as you wish or completely ignore it for it is too &quot;traditional and problematic&quot;.<br /> <br /> Each of those legacies I came up with are quite usefull but at the same time a problem maker. For a clear example, the verbena may do a single ritual on a storm without critical failure, but woundt It makes so much easier for the Technocracy to just do some heavy sourveilance to find a bunch of naked magi doing their ritual? Or on the One Song, it makes even easier to capture two birds with one shot, and damn If using it is flashy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","user":"menos125","date":". 05-30-2018, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T09:08:33-07:00","id":1223285,"title":"","content":"First, Attainments don't exist in Ascension to even compared them to Awakening. There's just no comparable system.<br /> <br /> Second, the problem with trying to make &quot;something unique but optional,&quot; in Ascension is extremely hard because of Backgrounds and Merits. Due to Ascensions desire to be as flexible as possible, almost any bonus you can think to make automatic in a Tradition, will basically just end up being a Merit or a Background other people could take anyway. Foundations are commonly cited as inspiration for making each Tradition more unique mechanically because it's easier to ensure they're more difficult to replicate by other means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T12:22:20-07:00","id":1223351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222926-mage-ascension-legacies?p=1223285#post1223285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, Attainments don't exist in Ascension to even compared them to Awakening. There's just no comparable system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my mistake, I should've used the word &quot;would&quot; in the phrase :<br /> <br /> &quot;The problem with Attainments is that they work in a very different way in Ascension than in Awakening&quot;.<br /> <br /> They way it is may induce someone understanding there is an Attainment system on Ascension which you're correct, there is not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222926-mage-ascension-legacies?p=1223285#post1223285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, the problem with trying to make &quot;something unique but optional,&quot; in Ascension is extremely hard because of Backgrounds and Merits. Due to Ascensions desire to be as flexible as possible, almost any bonus you can think to make automatic in a Tradition, will basically just end up being a Merit or a Background other people could take anyway. Foundations are commonly cited as inspiration for making each Tradition more unique mechanically because it's easier to ensure they're more difficult to replicate by other means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this one goes by storytellers discretion, I cant make it so that everyone follows the idea I had, and if they want to make it into a merit so should they, though I didnt think it as something you have to invest freebie points but something to be learned along gameplay and something a group would never share with others for social and political means as much as Akasha doesnt go on inviting everyone to Do classes.<br /> <br /> You did point something that bothers me in Ascension, you are free to create anything you desire for a character but at the cost of its uniqueness. Well, Paradigm is that thing that makes the character unique but being in a group should also be a factor that the game clearly doesnt work on. There is no big difference mechanically for a Hermetic, a Verbena or and Adept to cast a fireball, neither actually being in a Tradition does, its reduced to mere fluff.<br /> <br /> I dont love Awakening but damn if they did some good job at making a character both free customizable and with options to make it shine. Attainments have its flaws, but they are quite interesting, however they would never work on Ascension because: A) there are more than 150+ Legacies and thats because there are an enormous number of mages compared to Ascension; B) Attaintments are in its majority Effects cast without paradox.<br /> <br /> I think each group should have something that belongs intrinsically to each factions in the game, but not making it that strains free will, or using even more complex rules on an already convoluted system. I dont think my idea is perfect though, I myself criticize it a lot, but it makes it easier and &quot;clean&quot; as a house rule for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","user":"menos125","date":". 05-30-2018, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T12:26:44-07:00","id":1223353,"title":"","content":"And anyway, does anyone would like to contribute with an Idea for other Traditions, Conventions, Disparate, etc?<br /> Do as you wish, I would love to see some Ideas for other groups of better ones for those I already did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T13:21:52-07:00","id":1223374,"title":"","content":"My approach to this issue is to give each Tradition its own <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/88705-sphere-variants-for-the-traditions\">Sphere Variant(s)</a>, representing special knowledge that Tradition has uncovered about one or two of the Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:24:59-07:00","id":1223399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222926-mage-ascension-legacies?p=1223351#post1223351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well this one goes by storytellers discretion, I cant make it so that everyone follows the idea I had, and if they want to make it into a merit so should they, though I didnt think it as something you have to invest freebie points but something to be learned along gameplay and something a group would never share with others for social and political means as much as Akasha doesnt go on inviting everyone to Do classes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is the Do is neat... but really overrated. Martial Arts 3 (or higher with freebies), and a 1-dot Wonder that reduces your MA roll difficulties by -3 pretty much beats Do if you take a lethal attack as one of your MA maneuvers. And anyone can take it regardless of Tradition.<br /> <br /> Do's also a holdover from... a not great time in Mage's development that tended to fetishize Eastern cultural elements instead of represent them honestly. There's no reason why southeast Asian Mages would have a lock on 'the ultimate' martial art.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no big difference mechanically for a Hermetic, a Verbena or and Adept to cast a fireball, neither actually being in a Tradition does, its reduced to mere fluff. </div> </div> </div>But that's always been the point. Mechanically magical effect A is the same for everybody, even if in-character how they do it is all different. You don't need to learn a Hermetic fireball, vs. a Verbena fireball, vs. a VA fireball mechanically. Messing with that goes directly against the idea of making the game faster and/or lighter. The uniqueness comes on the Focus side of things (which M20 does offer a bunch of mechanics to tack on to), not the effect side of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attainments have its flaws, but they are quite interesting, however they would never work on Ascension because: A) there are more than 150+ Legacies and thats because there are an enormous number of mages compared to Ascension; B) Attaintments are in its majority Effects cast without paradox. </div> </div> </div>I think you're focusing too much on Legacy Attainments, and not enough of Awakening 2e's general Attainments. Things like Eyes of the Dead to let Chakravanti always be aware of any lingering ghosts around, or Honorary Rank to make spirit interactions easier for Dreamspeakers are fairly easy to port over from Awakening. Their might not be enough to cover ever Ascension faction, but there's a bunch of them and more than enough room to create similar effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:44:19-07:00","id":1223406,"title":"","content":"* peaks in after hearing something about Awakening\u2019s Legacies<br /> <br /> Like Heavy Arms said, Arcanum Attainments, which represent aptitude over the Arcana, could be easily adapted over as Sphere Attainments. Basically, if something requires N dots in Sphere X without being an Effect, it\u2019s likely an Attainment. I\u2019m not familiar enough with Ascension than I\u2019d like to be, so can\u2019t say much further. <br /> <br /> Legacy Attainments IC represent internalization of the Legacy\u2019s philosophy/worldview/theory on magic. A personalized Reality Zone? Between that, Foci, and Foundation, it\u2019s hard to come up with new things because magic already works like that (I think) in Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T08:59:15-07:00","id":1225303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222926-mage-ascension-legacies?p=1223406#post1223406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Heavy Arms said, Arcanum Attainments, which represent aptitude over the Arcana, could be easily adapted over as Sphere Attainments. Basically, if something requires N dots in Sphere X without being an Effect, it\u2019s likely an Attainment. I\u2019m not familiar enough with Ascension than I\u2019d like to be, so can\u2019t say much further.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not though. Magick in Ascension works only through effects. You can't see aspects of a sphere magically without an effect. You don't have resistance to a sphere's effects without an effect of your own. It really comes down to a fundamental difference in what magick IS between Ascension and Awakening. Magick in Ascension is an act of will that comes from within... it only exists because you will it to exist. Magick in Awakening is pulled from another realm into the mortal world and so can exist independent of the will to sustain it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Legacy Attainments IC represent internalization of the Legacy\u2019s philosophy/worldview/theory on magic. A personalized Reality Zone? Between that, Foci, and Foundation, it\u2019s hard to come up with new things because magic already works like that (I think) in Ascension. </div> </div> </div> Personal reality zones (that move with you) are basically what makes you a Marauder instead of a conventional mage. Again, it comes down the to the difference in how magic functions. Paradox in Awakening is because the magic is being corrupted by the Abyss as it being drawn into the mortal world; Attainments get around the Abyss to provide uncorrupted magic. Paradox in Ascension is the collective beliefs of humanity saying NOT POSSIBLE and slapping you for violating reality. You have to be a special kind of insane (i.e. a Marauder) to be able to create a personal reality bubble and even then they're only diverting the backlash of disbelief onto others and doing so too much actually pushes the Marauder further out of phase with conventional reality to the point that they can no longer exist inside reality.<br /> <br /> While both deal with transcending reality, Ascension and Awakening take essentially opposite directions on what that means. In Awakening you're uncovering deeper truths about the nature of reality and so able to find loopholes in the Exarchs version of reality you can exploit (i.e. Attainments); you gain power by cleaving more tightly to certain traditions. In Ascension you're evolving past your previous limits and advancement in magic comes from learning that the traditions you first learned are the things you must grow beyond... you gain more power by abandoning your traditions in favor of a more holistic perspective.<br /> <br /> They're basically exact opposites of each other in terms of worldview; at least in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T10:01:25-07:00","id":1225333,"title":"","content":"That's definitely the view of Ascension that the Traditions promote, yes. But as of M20, raising your Arete no longer means growing beyond your paradigm; it's just that among the Traditions, one's Paradigm tends to include what the Book of Secrets calls \u201cWe Are All Gods in Disguise\u201d, an ecumenical view of magick that, as it strengthens, tends to encourage the mage to look at all magick as being fundamentally the same. Outside of the Traditions, though, this view isn't nearly as common. Taking an extreme example, Technocrats generally <i>don't</i> subscribe to the WAAGID Paradigm. But it's not just the Technocracy; the various Crafts tend not to view magick in this way (and the exceptions, like the Batini and the Hollow Ones, used to be associated with the Traditions). <br /> <br /> If I were to try to import Attainments into Ascension, I'd probably use Mythic Threads and/or Earthly Foundations to justify them. Mythic Threads are basically \u201cminority views\u201d within the Consensus that are strong enough to support magick even when the majority view doesn't; and Earthly Foundations are aspects of Reality that are true regardless of what that Consensus says: M20 uses the latter to explain why certain Effects are always Vulgar even when there's widespread acceptance of them in the Consensus; but it can also be used to explain supernatural phenomena that are stubbornly resistant or even immune to influence by the Consensus. Mortal Sorcery is arguably a manifestation of Mythic Threads and/or Earthly Foundations; Attainments would be similar, but for the Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T10:05:57-07:00","id":1225335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222926-mage-ascension-legacies?p=1225303#post1225303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not though. Magick in Ascension works only through effects. You can't see aspects of a sphere magically without an effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening 1e had the same issue... but they managed to overcome it. Everything in Ascension is an effect because it has to be an effect because the game provides no other mechanism to express them; just like Awakening 1e. Awakening 2e realized it didn't have to do things that way, and built on the concept of Legacy Attainments in order to create a second category of magical aptitude that's more specialized control/applications of magic than unique effects.<br /> <br /> A simple example is the whole &quot;Forces does extra damage&quot; rule in Ascension. That's not an effect, that's not a spell, it's just a quirk that Forces gets despite it not really making an direct sense or follow every Focus' view of magic. In Ascension, it's just a rule hanging out there. In Awakening 2e, it's a Forces Attainment. This is the kind of space that Attainments could occupy (esp. as ways to make the different factions more mechanically distinct). For most mages Forces damage would be no better than any other damage, but for Hermetics, they can study their Tradition's secret Forces techniques for more damaging attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It really comes down to a fundamental difference in what magick IS between Ascension and Awakening. Magick in Ascension is an act of will that comes from within... it only exists because you will it to exist. Magick in Awakening is pulled from another realm into the mortal world and so can exist independent of the will to sustain it. </div> </div> </div>None of this is really relevant towards a discussion of mechanics one could use as inspiration from Awakening to help magic Ascension mage factions get more distinctive mechanical representations. This is easily demonstrated by the differences between Awakening 1e (where like Ascension, everything is an effect) and Awakening 2e (a lot of the meta-magic and 'this Sphere works a bit differently' stuff was moved over to be Arcana Attainment).<br /> <br /> Arcana Attainments can be representations of internal based magic, because they're based on trained skill in applying magic regardless of the source. Being more awesome than most mages at producing permanent Matter alterations rather than ones that undo after a short period of time because you've learned advanced treatment techniques as an Etherite doesn't conflict with Ascension's assumptions about the nature of magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paradox in Awakening is because the magic is being corrupted by the Abyss as it being drawn into the mortal world; Attainments get around the Abyss to provide uncorrupted magic. </div> </div> </div>This is a very 1e Awakening take on things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paradox in Ascension is the collective beliefs of humanity saying NOT POSSIBLE and slapping you for violating reality. </div> </div> </div>Any this just isn't true. You can still get Paradox for effects that don't violate Consensus, or when Consensus doesn't apply.<br /> <br /> In both games what you're citing as the 'source' of Paradox is what makes Paradox worse, not what causes it... the causes are actually pretty close here. Awakening 2e's cause of Paradox is the mage overreaching their ability to draw the Supernal into the Fallen, and the act of dragging that much power through the Abyss taints it with Paradox. Ascension's cause of Paradox is ultimately the mage bending reality too far for their abilities which causes a rebound in the form of Paradox, which is heightened by Consensus making certain effects more Paradox prone than others.<br /> <br /> Both games, while still highly divergent, put Paradox as a fundamental result of mages channeling too much power for reality to accept their actions without response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Awakening you're uncovering deeper truths about the nature of reality and so able to find loopholes in the Exarchs version of reality you can exploit (i.e. Attainments); you gain power by cleaving more tightly to certain traditions. </div> </div> </div>This is, again, a very 1e take on Awakening. 2e changes these assumptions considerably, though the second was never really true in either edition (there are bonuses to using traditions, with drawbacks for doing so, which isn't the same as it being a route to more power).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Ascension you're evolving past your previous limits and advancement in magic comes from learning that the traditions you first learned are the things you must grow beyond... you gain more power by abandoning your traditions in favor of a more holistic perspective. </div> </div> </div>But, M20 especially, challenges that interpretation quite significantly. M20 makes it clear that abandoning one's Instruments is not the same as transcending your traditional teachings. Ascension's few detailed Archmagi are not presented as having moved all in the same direction. If anything, they've all doubled down on their traditions heavily in their own personal ways. Porthos never stopped being a Hermetic, he never shed all those trappings, he just doesn't need them when push comes to shove (also, mechanically, you're still incentivized to use them anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T14:09:59-07:00","id":1225968,"title":"","content":"Hey, you guys actually made me think a bit and I may have come up with a more reasonable explanation for the legacies I had in mind. It comes down to the concept of the Consensus. Theoretically science is both the application of the Earthly Foundations and the result of humanity's imaginary of reality, the Consensus (I wonder if the Consensus can actually go against the Earthly Foundations, would be funny to see humanity at whole suffering from paradox without realizing such).<br /> <br /> Well my idea is that those legacies are actually the Consensus made by the mages themselves! You see, Sleepers can create the Consensus because at large they have a common belief, but what happens when Awakened does too have some common beliefs? Shouldnt it make sense that thos who actually can directly distort reality have also a passive effect of such alterations concocted by their collective thoughts? It does makes a lot of sense along the lines I try since, for example, the Choristers One Song does involve the idea that the emanation and representation of the One when more than one mage of such group tries to perform their magick is, in truth, what they believe it to be.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","user":"menos125","date":". 06-08-2018, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}